{"parentUuid":"de12109f-ed1b-466f-939b-d6a8b6127c84","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5fcae258-afae-4d15-9bce-94538261ed5d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a75a14c578badb121</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01KoqmGfCgpGURQdSYJLNstk</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-juks86-Downloads-myrealtrip-curator/7b24d798-2c5a-4e6e-ab7c-29d140386938/tasks/a75a14c578badb121.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Claude Code plugin marketplace git update mechanics\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Based on the official Claude Code documentation, here's the precise answer:\n\n## Local filesystem paths (`./src`)\nWhen your marketplace uses a local relative path like `\"source\": \"./src\"`, Claude Code **caches the plugin** when users install it (copies to `~/.claude/plugins/cache`). Edits to files in `./src` are **not** reflected live — users must reinstall or refresh the marketplace.\n\n## Git repository URLs\nIf you change the marketplace `source` to point to your GitHub repo (e.g., `\"source\": {\"source\": \"github\", \"repo\": \"giseungNoh/myrealtrip-plug-in\"}`), updates are **not automatic**. Users must manually run:\n- **In Claude Code**: `/plugin marketplace update` (or `/plugin marketplace update local` for your marketplace name)\n- **CLI**: `claude plugin marketplace update [name]`\n\nThis fetches the latest `marketplace.json` from the repo.\n\n## Version tracking\nIf you omit the `version` field in your plugin's `plugin.json`, every new git commit becomes a new version. Users get updates when they run `/plugin marketplace update`. If you set an explicit `version`, users only see updates when you increment it.\n\n## Automatic updates?\nThe docs don't mention session-start auto-polling or hooks to auto-sync. **Manual update is always required** regardless of source type. There's no way to make it fully automatic without user action.\n\n**Recommendation**: Use a git-based marketplace (`github` source) so users can run one command (`/plugin marketplace update`) to stay current, rather than reinstalling each time.\n\nFor the CLI equivalents, see: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/plugin-marketplaces.md#manage-marketplaces-from-the-cli</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>40478</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>5</tool_uses><duration_ms>34932</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"9ae8dc0f-f1ef-4562-8435-ddb5942698c5","timestamp":"2026-07-08T13:00:16.735Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/juks86/Downloads/myrealtrip-curator","sessionId":"357e1c4e-8991-4c27-8cb6-c71869e323bd","version":"2.1.198","gitBranch":"main"}
